now this is a story all about how will  smith's life got flip turned upside down  yes just like the prince of bel-air  smith's story has had some major twists  from rapper to slapper will smith is  never boring  you might be surprised to discover that  will smith's story actually doesn't  begin in film but in music performing as  dj jazzy jeff in the fresh prince smith  and his dj jeffrey townes were the first  ever recipients of a rap grammy for  1989's parents just don't understand the  duo picked up another trophy in 1991 for  summer time then came smith's solo music  career and men in black the song he  wrote for the movie earned him his third  grammy and in 1999 getting jiggy with it  scored smith grammy number four he's had  some nominations since then no small  feat but has put his music career on the  shelf to focus on acting for most people  four grammy wins and eight nominations  would be enough to retire for smith it  was a side project  will smith is no stranger to critical  bombs as his rotten tomato scores show  between wild wild west at 16 percent  bright at 27 and suicide squad at 26  these movies fall squarely into bomb  territory still it's hard to beat m  night shyamalan's 2013 sci-fi flop after  earth which received a rancid 12 on the  tomato meter ouch in this movie smith  plays a wounded father to a scared kid  played by his real-life son jaden set on  a hostile planet after a crash landing  it's hard to tell whether the acting  direction or screenplay was the worst  part of this film but for will the worst  part was almost certainly the backlash  against jaden who was just 14 at the  time smith told esquire that was a  valuable lesson for me a few years ago  with after earth that was the most  painful moment in my career  of course smith's rotten tomato numbers  aren't all bad men in black got 92  percent and king richard scored a 90.  after a successful run on the sitcom  fresh prince of bel air which ran for  six seasons from 1990 to 1996 smith got  the chance to prove he was more than a  rapper turned comedian by starring in  ali this 2001 biopic about legendary  boxer muhammad ali formerly known as  cassius clay follows ali's career from  the mid-60s to the mid-70s this was a  tumultuous period for the fighter during  which he won several iconic matches  while publicly commenting on hot-button  issues like the vietnam war and the  civil rights movement while ali didn't  break any box office records it was a  hit with critics demonstrated by this  rotten tomatoes critics consensus blurb  though perhaps no film could fully do  justice to the fascinating life and  personality of muhammad ali man's  direction and smith's performance  combined to pack a solid punch the role  also nabbed smith his first oscar  nomination for best actor in a leading  role it was proof that while he was  bankable as an action-comedy star he  could also hold his own with the best  when it came to drama  will smith was riding high at the end of  the 90s the fresh prince of bel air his  success in the music industry and his  leading man status in several  blockbusters had all turned him into a  household name but did you know he was  almost the star of another 90s franchise  maybe you've heard of it a little sci-fi  movie called the matrix  what is the matrix it is the world  that has been pulled over your eyes  that's right smith was almost neo but  the reason it didn't happen might  surprise you smith turned down the  matrix to star in wild wild west a  decision that seems a bit um misguided  in retrospect because while the matrix  is a beloved and thought-provoking  sci-fi gem wild wild west was a  forgettable bomb smith posted a youtube  video explaining what happened i did  turn down neo  in the matrix according to smith he was  a bit overconfident following the  success of independence day and probably  trusted his gut a little too much but he  isn't throwing any shade on the sci-fi  classic keanu was perfect lawrence  fishburne was perfect and as smith said  in the video it was all for the best i  probably would have messed the matrix up  i would have ruined it  will has always been a proud family man  including his kids and projects whenever  he can for example he starred with jaden  in a number of movies and while after  earth might have been a mistake the  pursuit of happiness certainly was not  in this 2006 movie smith stars as a  homeless man desperately trying to make  a better life for his son christopher  played by jaden according to rotten  tomatoes it was a critical favorite and  an excellent debut for jaden just eight  years old at the time will's on-screen  portrayal of a man who deeply loves and  wants the best for his son was clearly  genuine  the smiths seem to think the world is  clamoring for every detail of their  personal lives we ride together we die  together  bad marriage for life  but there's a fine line between open and  honest and really really awkward for  example in his memoir will goes into  excruciating detail about his sex life  with his wife jada pinkett smith saying  we had sex multiple times every day for  four straight months as far as i was  concerned there were only two  possibilities one i was going to satisfy  this woman sexually or two i was going  to die trying imagine being one of his  kids and reading that speaking of the  kids where do we even begin with red  table talk a facebook show in which jada  daughter willow and jada's mother adrian  banfield norris say things the public  really doesn't need to know geez this is  scary but it's real for example our  hosts discuss how willow learned about  sex after catching her parents in the  act and how um self-service has always  been a part of jada's life listen  transparency is cool but so is keeping  some things to yourself  while having famous parents certainly  gave smith's kids a big advantage this  doesn't mean jaden and willow aren't  talented in their own right and since  their success is also a win for will it  lands on the best category of our list  other than being a smith daughter willow  is most famous for her undeniably catchy  2010 single with my hair which peaked at  number 5 on the us pop charts as for  brother jayden he was featured on justin  bieber's 2010 song never say never which  peaked at number 8 on the billboard hot  100. never say never was the theme song  for the karate kid reboot with jackie  chan a film that jaden also starred in  and let's not forget that the pursuit of  happiness another movie he co-starred in  with his dad was a critical favorite  it's nice growing up rich to famous and  well-connected parents but fame's got a  darker side too and the smiths haven't  been immune to it buzzfeed had all the  details of a conversation smith had with  daughter willow who was touring europe  with justin bieber at age 10 to promote  her 2010 hit with my hair one day after  finishing her set and leaving the stage  willow said to will thank you daddy i'm  finished the ever professional smith  tried to convince his daughter to  complete her tour obligations to which  willow replied it doesn't matter to you  that i'm done daddy  it's a lot of work this question  affected will who realized his own  feelings had never been considered when  he was growing up he then realized he'd  been dropping similar baggage on his  daughter fortunately the encounter  changed his approach to parenting from  what he described as pushing and  prodding and cajoling people into the  vision that i had demanding that people  do the things i had envisioned for them  into something much different with smith  desiring to water and nourish and  nurture that seed to become what it  already is  now you might have realized that will  smith isn't in many billion dollar  blockbusters those seem to be reserved  for superhero movies these days and  smith's main attempt to get his foot in  that door resulted in suicide squad  hardly a badge of honor  oh not good  don't forget  we're the bad guys but that doesn't mean  he isn't bankable although only 2019's  aladdin made it to the one billion  dollar mark his cumulative box office  hall stretches far into the billions  business insider brought the receipts on  25 of the highest paid movie roles of  all time and will smith appears a few  times pulling in 40 million for king  richard and most impressively nabbing  the top spot with a 100 million paycheck  for his role as agent j in men in black  three  you know  yeah  we've already discussed the awkwardness  that is red table talk but the most  noteworthy incident by far had to be the  july 2020 episode when jada invited will  on the show to admit that the rumors  that she had cheated on him with rapper  august alcina were true she explained  that the affair happened because she and  will had been going through a rough  patch saying i just wanted to feel good  it had been so long since i felt good it  was really just a joy to just help heal  somebody even if you didn't watch the  bombshell episode you probably saw the  memes of will's face from the episode  where it looks like he's bursting at the  emotional seams even more embarrassing  while will referred to the incident as a  transgression that he's willing to look  past jada said i actually don't look at  it as a transgression at all  it's weird to even mention it in the  context of the now infamous slap that  preceded it by a few minutes but we do  need to note that will smith did take  away one of the top prizes at the 2022  academy awards best actor and it's not  like he didn't earn it smith received  massive acclaim for his portrayal of  richard williams the hard driving father  of tennis superstars venus and serena  williams venus and serena go shake up  this world on rotten tomatoes smith is  praised in the critic's consensus king  richard transcends sports biopic  formulas with refreshingly nuanced  storytelling and a towering performance  from will smith in the title role but  the slap overshadowed what should have  been a triumphant moment i want to  apologize to the academy i want to  apologize to all my fellow nominees art  imitates life i look like the crazy  father just like they said about richard  williams but love will make you do crazy  things you're gonna be the greatest of  all time he did get a standing ovation  when he was done but there would be  massive blowback to follow  the 2022 oscars should have been a slam  dunk for will but his best actor victory  was overshadowed by what occurred just  moments before in response to a joke  host chris rock made at jada pinkett's  expense a comment that touched on her  alopecia will stormed the stage and  slapped rock across the face any notion  that the incident was staged was put to  bed when smith shouted obscenities of  rock after returning to his seat it  immediately became one of the most  talked about moments in award season  history the fallout of the slap heard  around the world hit right after the  ceremony was over in an interview with  gail king  jim carrey said he was sickened by the  standing ovation smith received after  his oscar win smith did speak on  instagram the next day saying quote i  would like to publicly apologize to you  chris i was out of line and i was wrong  but as sincere as the apology may have  been consequences were inevitable the  bbc says that in april the academy of  motion picture arts and sciences elected  to ban smith for 10 years over the  incident while the new york post says  netflix and apple pulled out of a  bidding war for an upcoming will smith  biopic netflix has also pulled the plug  on a sequel to their 2017 hit film  bright which would have netted will  smith a hefty 30 million dollar payday  as you can see smith isn't just the king  of bel air he's also the king of the  career ups and downs will he make his  way back up to the top stay tuned to  find out  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite stuff are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

